THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================

Swiss Ephemeris
---------------
Astraea performs its astronomical calculations with the Swiss Ephemeris,
Copyright (C) 1997-2021 Astrodienst AG, Switzerland. The Swiss Ephemeris is
dual-licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 or a
commercial licence from Astrodienst AG.

Astraea uses it under the AGPL. Astrodienst requires that the Swiss Ephemeris be
credited in any software that uses it; that notice is displayed in the
application's About page as well as here.

  https://www.astro.com/swisseph/
  https://github.com/aloistr/swisseph

Astraea links the Swiss Ephemeris through sweph-wasm
(https://github.com/ptprashanttripathi/sweph-wasm), an Emscripten/WebAssembly
build of the Swiss Ephemeris C library.

Because the Swiss Ephemeris is AGPL and the AGPL's network clause applies to
software made available over a network, any deployment of Astraea that is
reachable by other people must offer those users the corresponding source code
of the running version. The application's About page carries that source link.

Ephemeris data files
--------------------
The compressed ephemeris data files shipped with this application
(sepl_18.se1, semo_18.se1, seas_18.se1) are derived from NASA/JPL's DE431
ephemeris and are distributed by Astrodienst AG as part of the Swiss Ephemeris
under the same terms.

